## Summary: 14 mutants, 12 killed, 2 survived.
## - strong_ge is killed by the guard of newton_step (the library aborts: from k0 = s the step does not raise
##   the precision); without the guard the mutant loops (timeout); with the guard gone and no lifting from
##   k <= s (strong_ge_nolift) the assertions fail: 5437230 failed checks in 7 tests.
## - (R1), (R2), (R3) each removed from the verifier: killed; the changed-list counts above show which kind of
##   change each condition refuses ((R1): the unreduced centre and (1, 1, 1) for X^2 + 3 at 2; (R2): s changed;
##   (R3): the centre moved and K raised).
## - plain_s_plus_1 and plain_2k SURVIVE and are equivalent: s = v_p(g'(a)) is at most the bit length of the
##   integer g'(a) held in memory, far below 2^62, so s + 1 cannot overflow; and k < K <= 2^22 after the limit
##   test 2 K bits(p) <= 2^24, so k + k cannot overflow. The one
##   operation that can overflow is the product of the limit test; its plain form (plain_limit_product) is
##   killed by prec_p = WORD_MAX / 2 + 1 at p = 2^64 - 59 (2 * 2^62 * 64 wraps to 0).

## after green (2026-09-29T11:10+02:00): a test of "LIMIT before any allocation" was added,
## limit_of_the_precision_is_decided_before_any_allocation: it counts the calls of FLINT's allocator
## (__flint_set_memory_functions, flint.h) during a call: an OK call makes 10, the LIMIT calls for
## prec_p = WORD_MAX at 7 and at 2^64 - 59 and for prec_p = 2^24 / 128 + 1 at 2^64 - 59 make 0. It was written
## after the code, so its red run is the mutant below (the first limit test removed, so that LIMIT comes from
## the core after g has been formed). GMP's own allocations of limbs and libc are not counted.

